# NOVAI @@NAME@@

@@DESCRIPTION@@

This tree was generated by the NOVAI meta-agent scaffolder from a spec. It follows the
two-key Type-10 funding model in `docs/AGENT_FUNDING_PLAYBOOK.md` and ships in DRY_RUN by
default. It is NOT ready for live until the data-source module and its parser test are
implemented (see the safety note below).

## Layout

```
bootstrap.py        one-time identity + faucet + register (DRY_RUN-safe)
oracle.py           the long-running loop (entry point)
lib/chain.py        the chain funnel (novai_sdk client + DRY_RUN path)
lib/signal.py       OracleAnchor construction + the generated observation encoding
lib/@@SOURCE_MODULE@@.py    data-source CONTRACT STUB (human implements the fetch)
lib/config.py       env parsing
lib/metrics.py      Prometheus registry
lib/log.py          structured logging
systemd/            unit + env template
tests/              structural tests + the failing-placeholder parser test
```

## Safety: the data source is a stub

`lib/@@SOURCE_MODULE@@.py` ships as a contract stub. `@@FETCH_FN@@` raises `NoDataError`
until a human implements the real read-only HTTP GET and parser. While it does, the loop
skips every cycle and posts nothing, so an unimplemented source cannot write to the chain.

`tests/test_@@SOURCE_MODULE@@_parser.py` ships as a failing placeholder. It stays red until
a human implements the parser and adds real fixture bytes. Do not enable live submission
while that test is red.

## Dry-run quickstart

```
python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install -e <repo>/sdk/novai-python-sdk
@@NS@@_DRY_RUN=1 @@NS@@_RUN_ONCE=1 .venv/bin/python oracle.py
.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests -q
```

## Deploy (human, supervised)

1. Implement `@@FETCH_FN@@` and make the parser test pass with real fixtures.
2. Review `REGISTER_PLAN.md` (the dry-run registration plan).
3. Install to `@@INSTALL_DIR@@`, copy the env template to `@@ENV_PATH@@` (mode 0600).
4. Run `bootstrap.py` (DRY_RUN first, then live) to register the entity.
5. Install the systemd unit, then `systemctl enable --now @@UNIT_NAME@@`.
6. Flip `@@NS@@_DRY_RUN=0` only after the parser test passes and the plan is reviewed.

Metrics are served on `http://127.0.0.1:@@METRICS_PORT@@/metrics`.
